# Frontend rules → backend validation

When the user asks for a **business rule, guard, or validation** on the JobseekerModule frontend (hide/disable actions, block navigation, form checks, progress/status gates, etc.), **also implement the same rule on the Bidding_* API** in the same change.

## Do

- Enforce the rule in the appropriate **service / repository / mutation guard** so clients cannot bypass the UI.
- Prefer shared helpers next to existing guards (e.g. `InterviewRecordMutationGuard`, lifecycle/readiness helpers) when the domain already has one.
- Return a clear **BadRequest** (or existing conflict pattern) with a user-facing message aligned with the UI intent.
- Keep exceptions that the product still needs (e.g. allow Send Results when edit is blocked) explicit in both layers.

## Do not

- Ship UI-only enforcement and leave the API open to the same mutation.
- Assume “frontend already blocks it” is enough for security or data integrity.

## Example

User: “If progress is 100%, don’t allow edit.”

- Frontend: hide Edit / redirect edit page.
- Backend: reject `PUT …/records/{id}` (and save-and-resend) when all scheduled seats are resolved, unless the call is an allowed completion transition (Send Results).
